$ terraform state list          # after the destroy stalled
aws_s3_bucket.this
aws_s3_object.readme
random_id.suffix

$ aws s3api list-object-versions --bucket devops-heros-dev-88bf5bd5
   version       welcome.txt 7dda6289-f84 latest
   version       welcome.txt 26976599-842
   delete-marker welcome.txt c6521a8b-49b

$ aws s3api delete-bucket --bucket devops-heros-dev-88bf5bd5
ClientError : An error occurred (BucketNotEmpty) when calling the DeleteBucket
operation: The bucket you tried to delete is not empty

# Versioning keeps EVERY version. The manual delete in the drift demo only added
# a delete marker, and Terraform's re-create wrote a second version. The bucket
# was never empty, so it could not be deleted.
